BenchForge

This project includes adapted simulator collectors, professional methods,
annotation clients/services, compiler algorithms and a reference template registry
from EurecaMoment/BenchClaw, https://github.com/EurecaMoment/BenchClaw,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Imported collectors: CARLA/quick_capture.py, HABITAT/collect_dataset.py,
LIBERO/collect_env_dataset.py. Machine-specific paths have been replaced with
explicit arguments, environment variables or the SDK's configured paths.
Template registry: BenchClaw/templates/template_library/benchforge_fixed_template_registry.json.
It is a knowledge reference, not an assertion that every template has an executable oracle here.

Bundled compiler and annotation code originates from revision 7299654 under the
upstream BenchClaw/ directory. Provenance and modifications are recorded in
src/benchforge_core/vendor/benchclaw/UPSTREAM.json; its Apache-2.0 license is retained.
Modifications include configured portable paths, flattened Windows packaging,
explicit service lifecycle, image-marker repairs and scorer contract integration.

DSH integration references the user's installed deepseek-harness runtime and
composes its installed preset definitions. DSH code, model weights, simulator
assets and datasets are not redistributed in this repository.

SpatialForge DSH tool definitions and delivery-review modules are imported from
the user-authorized SpatialForge working source (2026-09-29). Service execution,
acceptance rules and GT have not been changed by this client packaging.
